# Strings used only by the paste-warden command line (CLI, agent hooks, MCP). Prefix cli-.

## scan

cli-action-allow = No problems found
cli-action-warn = Needs attention
cli-action-quarantine = Dangerous: do not run or paste this
cli-level-none = none
cli-level-suspicious = suspicious
cli-level-malicious = malicious
cli-scan-command = Command verdict: { $level } (risk score { $score }/100)
cli-scan-reasons = Reasons:
cli-scan-trace = Deobfuscation steps:
cli-scan-hosts = Download hosts: { $hosts }
cli-scan-secrets = Secrets found (masked):
cli-scan-secret-item = { $label }: { $masked }
cli-scan-hidden = Hidden characters:
cli-scan-wallets = Found { $count } wallet address(es); check every character before pasting.
cli-scan-truncated = The input is long; only the first 1,048,576 characters were analyzed.
cli-error-read = Cannot read the input: { $cause }
cli-error-json = Line { $line } is not a JSON object with id and text.

## agent hook

cli-hook-deny-command = PasteWarden blocked this command: it was classified as malicious (risk score { $score }/100). Reasons: { $reasons }. Rewriting it will be blocked too; stop and tell the user.
cli-hook-ask-command = PasteWarden warning: this command may be risky (risk score { $score }/100). Reasons: { $reasons }. Ask the user to confirm before running it.
cli-hook-deny-content = PasteWarden blocked this tool call: the content contains a malicious command. Reasons: { $reasons }. Stop and tell the user.
cli-hook-deny-secret = PasteWarden blocked this tool call: it would send secrets out ({ $secrets }). Use the masked text instead, or let the user handle it.
cli-hook-ask-secret = PasteWarden warning: this command contains secrets ({ $secrets }). Ask the user to confirm before running it.
cli-hook-block-prompt = PasteWarden stopped this message before it reached the model: it contains secrets ({ $secrets }). Paste the masked version instead (paste-warden mask).
cli-hook-fail-closed = PasteWarden could not finish its check ({ $cause }) and blocked the call to stay safe. Tell the user.
cli-hook-cause-invalid-input = malformed hook input
cli-hook-cause-too-large = hook input too large
cli-hook-cause-panic = internal error
cli-hook-cause-timeout = check timed out

## hook install / uninstall

cli-install-dry-run = (--dry-run: showing the difference only; nothing was written)
cli-install-unchanged = Already installed, nothing changed: { $path }
cli-install-written = Written: { $path }
cli-install-backup = The previous file was backed up to: { $path }
cli-install-self-test-ok = Self-test passed: the malicious sample is blocked and echo hello is allowed.
cli-install-self-test-failed = Self-test failed: the hook did not decide as expected; do not rely on this installation.
cli-install-verify-claude = To verify: in Claude Code, ask the agent to run `echo hello` (it should run), then use the harmless sample in docs/integrations/agent-hooks.md to confirm blocking.
cli-install-verify-opencode = To verify: restart opencode, ask the agent to run `echo hello` (it should run), then use the harmless sample in docs/integrations/agent-hooks.md to confirm blocking.
cli-install-remove = To remove: paste-warden hook uninstall { $agent } --scope { $scope }
cli-install-not-json = { $path } is not a plain JSON object (comments or a syntax error?), so it was left unchanged. Add the settings by hand; see docs/integrations/agent-hooks.md.
cli-install-not-ours = { $path } exists but was not generated by PasteWarden; not overwritten.
cli-install-opencode-too-old = opencode { $version } is too old: the PasteWarden plugin needs opencode 2 or later (V2 plugin API).
cli-install-opencode-unknown = opencode was not found, so its version is unknown; the generated plugin only works with opencode 2 or later.
cli-uninstall-done = Removed the PasteWarden settings: { $path }
cli-uninstall-none = No PasteWarden settings found: { $path }

## MCP

cli-mcp-too-long = Input too long: the limit is 1,048,576 characters.
cli-mcp-redteam-later = The redteam profile arrives in Phase 5; only guard is available.
